# Galilean test for traveling pseudopotentials (electron translation factor).
# Isolated Ne atom (PseudoDojo PBE v0.4 standard Ne.psp8, 2 s + 2 p projectors)
# moving at constant velocity u = 0.5 a.u. along x in an empty box.
#
# The electrons are carried along by a constant uniform vector potential
# A = -u, which is a pure gauge boost: the exact solution is the at-rest
# ground state translated with the nucleus, and the total energy must stay
# exactly at E0 + N_e u^2/2 = E0 + 8 * 0.5^2 / 2 = E0 + 1 Ha at all times.
# This holds only if the nonlocal projectors travel with the atom
# (Stengel, Royo, Artacho, PRL 136, 196401 (2026)); see etf_kb.md.
#
# 1) ground state with the atom at rest
set cell 14 0 0 0 14 0 0 0 14 bohr
species neon Ne.psp8
atom Ne neon 0.0 0.0 0.0 bohr 0.5 0.0 0.0 atomicvelocity
set xc PBE
set ecut 40 rydberg
set ecutprec 4 rydberg
set force_complex_wf ON
set wf_dyn PSDA
set wf_diag T
set threshold_scf 1.E-10 5
randomize_wf
run 0 100 5

# 2) the atom moves at constant velocity (IMPULSIVE), electrons boosted by A = -u
set vector_potential -0.5 0.0 0.0
set atoms_dyn IMPULSIVE
set wf_dyn ETRS
set TD_dt 0.025 atomictime
set dt 0.025 atomictime
run 20 1
